		    RHIANTE'S BIO:<br>
Rhiante tries to be honorable at all times. She tries to help all in need without anything in return. She never asks money for the things she does, (it makes her feel guilty) but won't turn down donations if said person wants to donate. (She does need the donations sometimes). She is kind, and she never loot kills or exp kills. She rarely jumps into a fight, opting to heal the person as they fight rather than impose on their battle unless they are in dire need, or ask. However, she will always run towards a /yell for help and assist. She is sad when she can't make it in time and feels as if she's failed the person. (You people learn to yell before the last second!!). Rhiante is a group person or loner depending on her moods. At times she wants to solo only, others, she will gladly join a group, and will snare monsters and lightly buff group members and heal them. In group settings she has a lot of fun and is a team player. She is also quite light-hearted and jovial. She cannot stand a group that never talks, or is overly serious or is unfair or has bad leadership. Loot wise she never loots in a group. She's not in it for loot all the time. Although she does get annoyed at group members who loot all the time, or unfairly. She personally goes by either an alphabetical system or a dice rolling system. She will lead if asked but prefers to follow a fair leader. Fairness and justice and honor are what Rhiante lives by. <br>
<br>
FROM THE PLAYER:<br>
Rhiante is young. She is my highest character. I've been playing EQ for two months. Thus, she has no twinks or anything. Sometimes this makes me picky when helping people; because I always find myself broke. I try not to give money to people as I don't trust people asking for money. Instead I give them what I have, or forage them food or donate weapons or tailored armor. If I had a guild I would give to my other members, but out in the field it's hard to trust someone. I do dontate to newbies with no clue; be it a bit of armor or a bit of money. I hate a few things. People who beg. People who beg money to buy greedy ridiculous things. People who are mean or nasty to anyone (especially newbies). People who don't say thank you when you assist them or heal them. (Hey, a heal never goes astray even f you didn't necessarily want it, they were kind enough to!!). Also loathe heavily twinked characters who go around pompously or dueling other levels, or people affect the game because they're twinked. An example:  Someone who was level 7 went around smacking decaying skelletons for 30 damage all around halas to show off their weapon. They didn't win a lot of friends. Level ones and twos who needed exp with those easy kills got nothing. Someone else in Blackburrow pulled all the upper level gnolls onto himself, he was level 5. When my friend saw and assisted him by pulling one off, (thinking he needed help) the guy went savage and accused him of kill stealing, screaming his head off. It turned out he was heavily twinked, and wanted all the upper gnolls for himself. <br>
<br>
I hate peole like this. This to me is disrupting the game, the course of 'nature' because you're twinked waaaay too high for your level. It's fine if you're twinked and what you do doesn't effect anyone but you, but you are disrupting things when you train the gnolls onto yourself and hog them all causing the other levels who were hunting those things to go without. It's bad form, but these types do get their comeuppance.<br>
<br>
It's not necessarily the fact people are twinked, that bug me; it's what they do because of it. Hey, thats a good quote! "It's not your twink; it's how you use it."<br>
<br>
Anyway thats a bit of background on Rhiante and myself. Thanks to the people who are reading it. You're so kind to listen to my babble. Good hunting and may Lady Luck smile on you all.<br>


